<Layout
  title="Hyperion - Hardware - Rycode"
  description="Meta's Richland Parish, Louisiana campus: 5 GW of compute capacity, more than $50 billion, home of the Hyperion training cluster."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Hardware · Data center</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Hyperion</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">Hyperion is Meta's largest AI training cluster, a training cluster being the group of chips that teaches a model. It sits at Meta's data center in Richland Parish, Louisiana. On 13 July 2026 Meta raised the site to 5 GW of compute capacity, the largest in its fleet, and an investment of more than $50 billion (<a href="https://datacenters.atmeta.com/2026/07/deepening-our-investment-in-richland-parish-louisiana/">Meta, 13 Jul 2026</a>).</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Key figures</h2>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">Richland Parish data center</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Compute capacity</td><td>5 GW</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Investment</td><td>More than $50 billion</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ground broken</td><td>December 2024</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Construction jobs at peak</td><td>Over 7,500</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Jobs once running</td><td>1,000</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>A gigawatt (GW) is a billion watts, about the output of one large power plant; a megawatt (MW) is a thousandth of that. Data centers are sized by the power they can draw.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Power</h2>
    <p>Meta says its agreement with Entergy, the local utility, funds seven new natural gas plants, three grid-scale batteries, nuclear uprates (upgrades that let an existing reactor produce more), and other purchased power. Meta also commits to help fund up to 2.5 GW of clean and renewable energy and says it will match all of the site's power use with clean energy. Meta puts the customer savings at about $2 billion, on top of $650 million announced earlier. These are Meta's figures.</p>
    <h2 class="ai-model-section">What is not public</h2>
    <p>Meta has not named the chips or the chip count for Hyperion in the post cited here.</p>
    <p>Meta's other big cluster is <a href="/ai/hardware/data-centers/prometheus/">Prometheus</a> in Ohio.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://datacenters.atmeta.com/2026/07/deepening-our-investment-in-richland-parish-louisiana/">Meta, Deepening our investment in Richland Parish (13 Jul 2026)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
